# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
# Anchor the binary-name ignores so they don't also hide directories
# named "vornik" elsewhere in the tree (e.g. deployments/helm/vornik/).
/vornik
/vornikctl
/vornik-images

# Build output directory
/bin/
/.bin/

# Packaging artifacts — rpm/deb/checksums live only in dist/ (ignored below) or
# as release assets; they are NEVER committed. scripts/check-no-binaries.sh
# guards this in CI.
*.rpm
*.deb
# Generated FULL_ARCH goreleaser config (scripts/package-enterprise.sh)
/.goreleaser.enterprise.full.*.yaml

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
# ...but NOT the agent-tool dispatch goldens, which are recorded tool OUTPUT
# and end in .out. This rule swallowed all 64 of them for a week (2026-09-05):
# the golden passed on the recording machine and CI had no fixtures at all.
# test/agent/fixtures_tracked_test.go fails if a fixture is ever ignored again.
!test/agent/fixtures/**/*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# Node.js
node_modules/
package-lock.json
package.json

# .env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
.codex

# Python service build artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
/skills-site

# Local dev runtime state (make dev → configs/vornik.io.yaml)
/.dev/
/dist/

# Superpowers brainstorming visual companion (local mockups)
.superpowers/

# Local Claude Code config + worktrees (per-machine settings, permissions, agent state)
.claude/

# Phase 2b public-CE export output (scripts/export-public-ce.sh)
.vornik-export/

# Local working clones used by the CE-export + site-publish scripts
.vornik-public-clone/
.vornik-site/

# Root build artifacts (go build ./cmd/... lands the binary at repo root).
# One entry per cmd/ directory — a missing name means `go build ./cmd/x` leaves an
# untracked binary in the tree, which `make check-no-binaries` is there to catch.
/vornik
/vornik-enterprise
/vornikctl
/vornik-broker
/agent-helper
/docs-gen
/lint-lld-contracts
/mcp-bridge
/reachability
/skills-site
/ui-smoke

# make reachability-map output (a local analysis artifact, regenerated on demand)
/build/

# mkdocs local build output (published from CI / manually to vornik-docs gh-pages)
site/

# LongMemEval haystacks — 15 MB (oracle) and 265 MB (_s), fetched from
# huggingface.co/datasets/xiaowu0162/longmemeval-cleaned (v1-cleaned, Sept 2025).
# Never committed: the comparability key pins the revision by dataset_sha256, so
# the file is reproducible from its digest rather than from our history.
bench/longmemeval/*.json

# Benchmark run output: journals, manifests, results. Large, machine-generated,
# and pinned by hash in the artifacts that reference them — never committed.
# An untracked run directory also stamps vcs.modified=true on any binary built
# afterwards, and `bench agent run` refuses a harness it cannot regenerate from
# a commit, so leaving these unignored breaks the next benchmark pass.
/bench-runs/
/agentbench-runs/
/membench-runs/
